1. Lucide — `gamepad-2` icon (ISC)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Upstream: https://lucide.dev  ·  https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
    License:  ISC
    Full text: THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/Lucide-ISC.txt
    Used in:  assets/brand/ksx-detailed.svg  (the two pad silhouettes)

The ksx brand mark's two overlapping gamepads are Lucide's `gamepad-2` BODY
path, filled and outlined rather than stroked as Lucide draws it, placed at
`translate(29.4 5) scale(.8)` and `translate(40.4 12.5) scale(.8)` in the
64×64 mark. The path data is reproduced verbatim in that file.

Everything downstream of that SVG carries the path too, because it is all
generated from it by `tools/icongen`:

    assets/brand/dist/ksx-{48,64,128,256}.png
    assets/brand/dist/apple-touch-icon.png
    assets/brand/dist/ksx-256.rgba          (the egui cabinet window icon)
    assets/brand/dist/ksx.ico               (its 48/64/128/256 entries)
    crates/ksx-studio/brand/favicon.ico     (a copy of ksx.ico)

and, from there, the `.ico` compiled into `ksx.exe` as a Win32 resource
(`crates/ksx-app/build.rs`).

The simplified mark — `assets/brand/ksx-simple.svg`, and therefore the
16/20/24/32 `.ico` entries, the same-sized PNGs and `favicon.svg` — contains
NO Lucide geometry: at those sizes the silhouette is gone anyway and the pads
are plain rounded rectangles.

